---
import Article from "../layouts/Article.astro";
import PayGrid from "../components/PayGrid.astro";
const toc = [
  { id: "methods", label: "Payment methods" },
  { id: "deposit", label: "How to deposit" },
  { id: "verify", label: "Verification" },
  { id: "withdraw", label: "How to withdraw" },
  { id: "times", label: "Fees and timing" },
  { id: "problems", label: "If a payment is delayed" },
];
---

<Article
  cover="deposit-withdrawal"
  title="Pocket Option Deposit & Withdrawal: Methods, Fees, Times"
  description="Deposit from $5 with 170+ payment methods and withdraw with no Pocket Option fees. Cards, e-wallets, crypto, verification and payout times explained."
  h1="Pocket Option deposits and withdrawals"
  lead="Deposits start at $5 and Pocket Option charges no commission either way. Here is how to fund your account, get verified and withdraw without delays."
  crumb="Deposits & withdrawals"
  toc={toc}
>
  <h2 id="methods">Payment methods</h2>
  <p>
    Pocket Option lists more than 170 payment methods. What you see in your account depends on your country and
    currency.
  </p>
  <PayGrid />
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Cards:</strong> Visa, Mastercard and local card schemes.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>E-wallets:</strong> Jeton, Volet, WebMoney, Apple Pay, Google Pay, Paytm, GrabPay and more.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Bank transfers and QR:</strong> UPI, QRIS, DuitNow, VietQR, PSE and other local rails.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Mobile money:</strong> M-Pesa, MTN, Airtel, Orange, Vodacom and others across Africa.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Crypto:</strong> Bitcoin, Ethereum, USDT on several networks, Litecoin, Tron, Solana and more.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="deposit">How to deposit</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Log in and open <strong>Finance → Deposit</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>Choose a payment method and enter the amount, from $5 for most methods.</li>
    <li>
      Add a promo code if you have one. Read its conditions first, see{" "}
      <a href="/bonus-promo-code/">bonus and promo codes</a>.
    </li>
    <li>Confirm the payment with your provider. Most deposits are credited within minutes.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="verify">Verification</h2>
  <p>
    Verification protects your account and is required before you can withdraw. Pocket Option asks for your personal
    details, a photo ID and, in some cases, proof of address. Verifying right after registration saves time later.
  </p>
  <div class="note">
    Use your real name and details from the start. A mismatch between your profile and your documents or payment method
    is the most common reason for a delayed withdrawal.
  </div>

  <h2 id="withdraw">How to withdraw</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Open <strong>Finance → Withdrawal</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>Select a method you used to deposit. Anti-money-laundering rules require funds to return the same way.</li>
    <li>Enter the amount and confirm.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Pocket Option sets no minimum or maximum withdrawal amount when you have no active deposit bonus. If a bonus is
    still active, its amount is deducted from your balance when you withdraw.
  </p>

  <h2 id="times">Fees and timing</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Method</th>
        <th>Deposit</th>
        <th>Withdrawal arrival</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Crypto</td>
        <td>Minutes, after network confirmations</td>
        <td>Usually within a day</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>E-wallets</td>
        <td>Instant to minutes</td>
        <td>Usually within a day</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Mobile money, local transfers</td>
        <td>Instant to minutes</td>
        <td>Same day to a few days</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Bank cards</td>
        <td>Instant</td>
        <td>Several business days</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Pocket Option charges 0% on deposits and withdrawals. Your bank, card issuer or the blockchain network may still
    charge their own fees or apply a currency conversion rate.
  </p>

  <h2 id="problems">If a payment is delayed</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Check that your account is fully verified.</li>
    <li>Make sure you are withdrawing to a method you used to deposit.</li>
    <li>Check whether an active bonus is affecting your balance.</li>
    <li>Contact Pocket Option support from your account with the transaction ID.</li>
  </ul>
</Article>
